error: a bare `T` has no methods
  --> methods.norn:35:5
   |
35 |     value.to_string()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `to_string` called on a type parameter
   = note: `T` is opaque inside `describe`: without a bound it can only be moved, stored, matched by binding, or passed on

error: I64 has no method `Empty`
  --> methods.norn:42:19
   |
42 |     let a = Shape.Empty()
   |                   ^^^^^ no impl provides it
   = note: a method comes from a trait: an `impl` with a `fn Empty` taking I64 is what declares one

error: I64 has no method `frobnicate`
  --> methods.norn:44:15
   |
44 |     let b = 7.frobnicate()
   |               ^^^^^^^^^^ no impl provides it
   = note: a method comes from a trait: an `impl` with a `fn frobnicate` taking I64 is what declares one

error: `name` is a field of User, not a method
  --> methods.norn:47:18
   |
47 |     let c = user.name()
   |                  ^^^^ fields hold values; they cannot be called
   = note: an `impl` is what gives a type methods

error: I64 has more than one method named `shout`
  --> methods.norn:49:15
   |
49 |     let d = 3.shout()
   |               ^^^^^ ambiguous method
   = note: `Loud` provides one
   = note: `Quiet` provides one
   = note: methods share one name and functions do not: call the function form the impl delegates to
